{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta","id":1514544,"title":"What's the point of the resource background in mta?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-10T20:41:13-07:00","id":1514544,"title":"What's the point of the resource background in mta?","content":"Since pc's can simply use magick to help generate wealth, such as using entropy and time to help play the stock market, why would players want to take resources as a background and not invest in something different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T21:11:38-07:00","id":1514546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta#post1514544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since pc's can simply use magick to help generate wealth, such as using entropy and time to help play the stock market, why would players want to take resources as a background and not invest in something different?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all decisions are mechanically optimal. Some are for flavour, to fit the character background, to give some material to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Also, some paradigms are predicated on the power that money grants. It is hard to use that power if you lack the means initially.<br /> <br /> <br /> Think of Hypereconomics, it will be hard to be &quot;<i>the man of means and power</i>&quot; without starting with certain abilities and backgrounds, Resources among those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-11-2023, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T22:32:46-07:00","id":1514549,"title":"","content":"Also, if the PCs are consistently generating wealth over time, that would reasonably take the form of Resources dots on their sheets that they had earned through actions in-game, I would think. Even if they did not start with Resources, they would have them eventually. Backgrounds are things that characters often acquire through IC actions rather than spending experience points, though that can be an option sometimes.<br /> <br /> But also, setting aside the excellent point about the role Resources might play in a Focus, characters who convert their magical aptitude into enormous piles of cash are going to draw attention of some kind or another, especially if they start throwing it around. Having access to a mundane source of finances that isn't going to look suspicious can be valuable in itself, depending on your goals.<br /> <br /> A Mage can count on being able to easily scrounge up enough money for a sparse but comfortable lifestyle without too much trouble. But if you want the kind of money that lets you shape communities, then simply magicking it up has a lot of potential to backfire. That's not something you have to worry about if you happened to inherit the Wayne family fortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T05:39:43-07:00","id":1514572,"title":"","content":"Also Mages generally avoid being too obvious. By creating plausible deniablity a Mage can hide in plain sight. Someone who owns a large house and has no visible means of support stands out and inspires curiosity. Mages generally need space and privacy. Someone with a large bank account can have an isolated space of their own without exciting any special notice.<br /> <br /> Yes, some Mages live outside of the economy. But many more prefer camouflage. Besides, when a Mage needs to travel among the Sleepers, having a check card backed by a bank account and paid off credit cards with substantial credit limits is massively convenient. The Heremetic living in a large old house at the edge of the suburbs becomes just another old dude with cash when that cash is in the public records. The Verbena Witch becomes just another weirdo cat lady left an annuity by her parents with the Resources background. The Sahajiya jazz man with a small Jazz label is just another Sun-Ra wannabe, falling below the notice of the Technocratic Union.<br /> <br /> Resources are a useful mask and a flexible tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-03-2023, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T10:48:05-07:00","id":1514583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta#post1514544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since pc's can simply use magick to help generate wealth, such as using entropy and time to help play the stock market, why would players want to take resources as a background and not invest in something different?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of at least a few reasons to get the background at char creation: if it's part of focus, if the mage doesn't have a way to get tons of money magickally and if the mage doesn't want to suddenly draw attention or doesn't want to deal with the effort and trouble of getting rich over night.<br /> <br /> Not all spheres can get you rich easily. While Time and Entropy are good ways, and Matter and Forces could create or the illusion of real gold, idk how Life, Prime or Correspondence could do that with such ease.<br /> <br /> Also, as others posted, you might draw attention of the Crats or sleeper government if you get a lot of money quickly, depending on how it's done.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are also mundane ways of doing it, like using computer to hack accounts and get tons of money. However, a failure means you might be a wanted criminal, and even a success could put you on the spotlight.<br /> <br /> Anyway, from a efficiency point of view, resources isn't a good way of spending bg points. But I believe that's true gor all splats, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T12:01:59-07:00","id":1514595,"title":"","content":"Because it fits my character's concept. And because it is less likely to risk any sort of Paradox if it fails.<br /> <br /> (Malcolm Shepherd once suggested the idea that any time a Mage uses magic to acquire something mundane, like money or catching a cab or getting a hotel room, through &quot;luck&quot; or happenstance, they are likely taking something that otherwise would have gone to a normal person, possibly interfering with their destiny.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:25:37-07:00","id":1514733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1514595#post1514595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it fits my character's concept. And because it is less likely to risk any sort of Paradox if it fails.<br /> <br /> (Malcolm Shepherd once suggested the idea that any time a Mage uses magic to acquire something mundane, like money or catching a cab or getting a hotel room, through &quot;luck&quot; or happenstance, they are likely taking something that otherwise would have gone to a normal person, possibly interfering with their destiny.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just that. There's an amazing number of problems money can solve. No risks or supernatural backlash involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:05:55-07:00","id":1514756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1514733#post1514733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not just that. There's an amazing number of problems money can solve. No risks or supernatural backlash involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It's one of the reasons I like to use the background pinnacles concept from the original edition of Adventure rather than going from 6 to 10. I think there comes a point where you are so wealthy that the exact number doesn't matter, and you can just afford to buy any equipment or service in the game. (The Adventure bit was called Wealth Beyond Avarice. I started calling the Mage one Balance Unlimited, after the anime of the same name.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:27:47-07:00","id":1514760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1514756#post1514756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. It's one of the reasons I like to use the background pinnacles concept from the original edition of Adventure rather than going from 6 to 10. I think there comes a point where you are so wealthy that the exact number doesn't matter, and you can just afford to buy any equipment or service in the game. (The Adventure bit was called Wealth Beyond Avarice. I started calling the Mage one Balance Unlimited, after the anime of the same name.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Me too! I've been using those instead of the 6+ ratings from GttTech and onwards <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T18:20:19-07:00","id":1515438,"title":"","content":"Resources isn't just having money. It's the sum total of one's money, physical possessions (beyond what the character is wearing or carrying at the time), and their living situation (housing, access to transport, etc).<br /> <br /> If you have Resources 0, you either live in someone else's home, or are unhoused. Anyone who has spent any time without housing knows that that can be a knock-on effect on every other aspect of your life. (Although at the same time, there's people who are fully employed, but still can't afford housing. But that's a problem of our bass-ackwards economic system and housing/renting market). You have to find ways to keep your clothes clean, or people won't give you the time of day. (If they don't just call the cops, which can be as good as a death sentence if the cops or even passers by feel like <i>committing murder</i> that day). You have no car, which is either a debilitating handicap (in America) or a non-issue (most every other industrialized country). You may not even be able to walk into a store or fast food joint and buy something, without your ability to do so being in severe question. (So, if you need a tool from a hardware store to solve a problem, you might not be able to afford it. Same with lunch, which might leave your character hungry during key moments...or most of the time.)<br /> <br /> A Mage without Resources must basically rely on either the help of others (like fellow PCs) or constant use of Magick to accomplish goals (which carries its own risks, as established).<br /> <br /> At a certain point, the amount of extra problems having no Resources generates would be more of a hassle than just...investing a single dot into the Background. If you're using Magick to acquire money needed to get by, you'll probably end up getting Resources 1 during the game anyway.<br /> <br /> Playing a magical hobo is a time-honored tradition in Mage. But unless that's the character concept (or at least the campaign start) you're going for, you're just tying one hand behind your back for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T19:33:50-07:00","id":1515442,"title":"","content":"More generally: Resources provides a game system representing how much wealth you have access to. This can be useful in the game in a number of ways: you could, for instance, implement a rule where you can use Magick to temporarily boost a Background; which is essentially what the original poster was suggesting in terms of \u201cjust use Magick to play the stock market whenever you need a quick buck.\u201d Just keep in mind that a mage who is constantly using Magick to boost his Resources is in the same boat as the mage who is always using Magick to boost his Strength: yes, you get the boost; but the fact that you're having to use Magick every time you want it is going to have consequences \u2014 and likely sooner rather than later. If you want <i>reliable</i> access to Resources, take the Background; just like if you want reliable access to the benefits of high Strength, raise your Strength.<br /> <br /> And the flip side of Magick and Resources is that there's at least one Magical Practice where Resources are effectively an Instrument: the Art of Desire, or Hypereconomics. Heck, access to Ventures is only <i>possible</i> for those with Resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-18-2023, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T09:32:54-07:00","id":1515674,"title":"","content":"The thing is that you can get tons of money one time and go from there. And if done right, probably wont need to do it again.<br /> it also doesn't have to be created from magick, although using magick to help accomplishing this might be easier. <br /> In a time where all ppl finances are numbers on a screen, one could achieve that by using computer skills alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T11:42:08-07:00","id":1515681,"title":"","content":"The thing about Backgrounds is that most of them are designed to change according to what happens in the narrative. Get a sudden windfall that's going to leave you set for life? You're Resources Background goes up accordingly. Suffer a setback that wipes you or financially? Your Resources Background drops accordingly. <br /> <br /> At least, that's one way to handle it. Another way is to treat the Background as a meta-narrative element: it serves as an indication to the Storyteller of how you want your character to relate to the world, and as such establishes a story of status quo that you're character might temporarily deviate from, but will tend to return to. In this view, someone with no Resources who attempts to acquire a windfall through Magick will succeed, for a time; but events will conspire to burn away the additional money that he has above and beyond his Resources rating. Unless and until he raises his Resources Background to match his newfound wealth, the new funds will always be in some sort of jeopardy until he loses them. <br /> <br /> Conversely, a character with a high Resources score who suffers a Syndicate attack that wipes him out will have to deal with the loss of his financial well-being for a time; but as long as the high Resources Background is on the character sheet, he'll have an easier time getting back to his accustomed level of wealth than someone without the same Resources Background would be able to manage. Play out the story arc, then reset to the status quo. Or, if the status quo is permanently changed to one where you have a lower Resources Background overall, redistribute the Background dots from Resources to another, compensatory, Background. For instance, you lose your wealth, but you make new friends: trade dots of Resources for dots of Allies. <br /> <br /> This second approach works better when you treat Backgrounds as something that you purchase with experience points, whereas the first approach works better when you <i>don't</i> attach xp costs to Backgrounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T13:29:13-07:00","id":1515687,"title":"","content":"Afaik, backgrounds cannot be bought with xp...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T14:57:31-07:00","id":1515694,"title":"","content":"There's an optional rule in M20, adapted from MRev, that lets you charge xp for Backgrounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:14:27-07:00","id":1515754,"title":"","content":"Also because a lot of mages have unawakened family that they even potentially had before awakening. And Jobs. And friends they hang out with after a long day of studying. And a modern upbringing they cling to. Or even their own business. And, and, etc...<br /> <br /> The question is not 'why take resources in chargen'. That is the wrong direction of building a character from start to finish.<br /> The question is 'Would this character, based on their history, life environment and current situation have a resources rating?'<br /> <br /> The stats should represent the character you come up with, instead of the character representing the stats you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T17:30:42-07:00","id":1515808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1515754#post1515754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also because a lot of mages have unawakened family that they even potentially had before awakening. And Jobs. And friends they hang out with after a long day of studying. And a modern upbringing they cling to. Or even their own business. And, and, etc...<br /> <br /> The question is not 'why take resources in chargen'. That is the wrong direction of building a character from start to finish.<br /> The question is 'Would this character, based on their history, life environment and current situation have a resources rating?'<br /> <br /> The stats should represent the character you come up with, instead of the character representing the stats you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, bu this reasoning, every char should have at least 2 or 3 dots in resources. Unless you are a hobo mage, which probably isn't a majority. <br /> I Don't like the idea that a background is mandatory for the char to function, that's my problem with resources...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T01:18:37-07:00","id":1515827,"title":"","content":"That's a complaint I can get behind. Resources is awkward in that regard, in that I can't think of any other Background where not having it puts you at a distinct disadvantage relative to the Hypothetical Average Person. One way to address this is to recalibrate Resources so that what's currently 2 dots becomes 0 dots. I\u2019d keep 5 dots the same, spread what's currently 3 or 4 dots over the one-to-four for range (3 becomes 1 or 2; 4 becomes 3 or 4; and two new levels get interpolated), and replace what's currently 0 or 1 dot with a Flaw representing poverty. Another way to address it is to just give everyone two dots in Resources at character creation; though that runs into the problem of what to do if someone wants to play a hobo mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T01:36:34-07:00","id":1515830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1515827#post1515827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another way to address it is to just give everyone two dots in Resources at character creation; though that runs into the problem of what to do if someone wants to play a hobo mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The solution is negative backgrounds. We've had them in Mage before. Simply reset Zero as you suggested and make the old Zero a level of negative background granting points from a flaw. Being dead broke would be a three point flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T03:32:56-07:00","id":1515842,"title":"","content":"<b>M20 Book of Secrets</b> took the Adversarial Backgrounds from <b>Guide to the Traditions</b> and recast them as Flaws, on the grounds that Adversarial Backgrounds had only ever appeared in that one book. That's why I didn't suggest an Adversarial Background; but also, there's already Debts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T12:11:36-07:00","id":1515882,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you necessarily need to have Resources 0 represent rock-bottom, just precariousness. You can make just enough money to cover a small apartment in the worst part of town, or a room in someone else's place somewhere nicer, but you have no real savings for a rainy day, just one week of missed work away from losing it all. Maybe you have a car, but it's some clunky beater that could die anytime, and you don't have the money to fix it. That makes Resources 0 less of an active penalty and more of a &quot;this isn't a great place to start, but it probably isn't going to active kneecap you if you're smart.&quot; Or you can simply embrace the hobo life if that's what you're going for.<br /> <br /> Being unhoused and jobless against your will might be better represented as a genuine Flaw, even if it's just something that would indirectly impair your ability to get steady work which would then result in you not being able to keep a roof over your head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T13:05:18-07:00","id":1515887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1515882#post1515882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if you necessarily need to have Resources 0 represent rock-bottom, just precariousness. You can make just enough money to cover a small apartment in the worst part of town, or a room in someone else's place somewhere nicer, but you have no real savings for a rainy day, just one week of missed work away from losing it all. Maybe you have a car, but it's some clunky beater that could die anytime, and you don't have the money to fix it. That makes Resources 0 less of an active penalty and more of a &quot;this isn't a great place to start, but it probably isn't going to active kneecap you if you're smart.&quot; Or you can simply embrace the hobo life if that's what you're going for.<br /> <br /> Being unhoused and jobless against your will might be better represented as a genuine Flaw, even if it's just something that would indirectly impair your ability to get steady work which would then result in you not being able to keep a roof over your head.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Resources zero was portrayed, though. It's a direct measure of any possessions you may have. And it's not like there are whole factions in the game who live off the grid, getting by through their own skills and self sustenance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T06:52:20-07:00","id":1515944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1515887#post1515887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how Resources zero was portrayed, though. It's a direct measure of any possessions you may have. And it's not like there are whole factions in the game who live off the grid, getting by through their own skills and self sustenance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't paid close attention to Resources as a Background to be honest, so I have quite possibly missed things, but that was never quite the vibe that I got. It's always come across more to me that you're allowed to have some modest Things without any Resources, but Resources is a safety net, and what lets you get more Things you need without any muss or fuss.<br /> <br /> And yes, I definitely don't think that Resources 0 is some inescapable blight on a character. That was why I said being homeless and jobless <b>against your will</b> should probably be represented as a Flaw of some kind, rather than the idea of treating Resources 0 itself like a Flaw, which seemed to be the vibe of some of the previous posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T15:44:01-07:00","id":1515972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 100%\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">X</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Working Poor: you live paycheck to paycheck, and that's about it.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Slightly ahead of the game: you've got a small apartment and perhaps a cheap vehicle.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Lower middle class: you've got a condo or apartment, plus a vehicle, some savings, and enough money for occasional indulgences.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Middle class with property: you either own or have decent equity in some property, plus a vehicle, investments, and savings. You could maintain a one-dot standard of living indefinitely.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Well-off: You own a large house, some property, and at least two vehicles, as well as notable levels of savings and investments. By local standards, you're a millionaire, and although that's not worth as much as it once was, it's nothing to sneeze at.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Welcome to the 1%. As a multimillionaire, you've got substantial holdings, investments, and savings.</td> </tr> </table></div> Implicit in this is that if you don't have even one dot, you don't even have an apartment. Unless you're living at a friend's or family's house, you're homeless. <i>That</i>, IMHO, ought to be a Flaw; even at zero dots of Resources, a character ought to have enough to have a place to stay. Basically, \u201cyou've got a small apartment and perhaps a cheap vehicle\u201d doesn't strike me as \u201cslightly ahead of the game\u201d; it feels more like \u201cthe working poor\u201d. Ditto for the descriptions given for two, three, and four dots: the labels work fairly well; but the descriptions of what those labels supposedly mean feel like they ought to go with the next ranking down. Except for Well-off: the first part (owning a large house, some property, and at least two vehicles, as well as notable levels of savings and investment) feels more like Middle class with property, whereas the second part (\u201cby local standards, you're a millionaire, and although that's not worth as much as it once was, it's nothing to sneeze at\u201d) feels appropriate to \u201cWell-off\u201d. <br /> <br /> This comes from personal experience: I have a friend who owns a house that eight people can live in comfortably (two stories and a basement, with three bedrooms upstairs, one downstairs, another room converted into a bedroom downstairs, and the basement converted into effectively a luxury apartment), and two cars; and he's got decent levels of savings and investments \u2014 all the earmarks of what Resources is calling Well-off, except that he's far from being a millionaire. He feels more like Middle class with property. (Part of that is that of the right people living there, one is his wife and four are his children.)<br /> <br /> Likewise, my own situation is what I would call \u201cworking poor\u201d: I'm renting a room (in effect, an apartment), and I have access to a vehicle for use on the job; with luck, I'll be in a position to buy a cheap vehicle for myself in about six months or so. I would consider my current situation to be the bottom of the Resources chart, the X; and the car won't change that.<br /> <br /> Six months ago, I was staying in a shelter, because things got <i>really </i>bad for me; without the shelter, I would have been living on the streets. It was <i>worse</i> than \u201cworking poor\u201d. <br /> <br /> That said, I also knew a guy who <i>was</i> living on the streets; and as bad as things were for me in that shelter, they were far worse for him. So perhaps the \u201csub-X\u201d should come in at least two levels: homeless (you're somehow able to find a room to sleep in every night; but it's an ongoing challenge, and there's no guarantee that it will be the <i>same</i> room) and destitute (if you're lucky, you're pitching a tent in the local park; if not, you're sleeping in a cardboard box).<br /> <br /> Before things fell apart for me and landed me in that shelter, I was living in an apartment, with a vehicle of my own, some savings, and enough money for the occasional indulgence \u2014 and I didn't feel \u201clower middle class\u201d; I felt \u201cslightly ahead of the game\u201d. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> So if I were reworking the Resources table, I'd bump X down to a Flaw (possibly with two levels: homeless and destitute), \u2022 down to X, \u2022\u2022 down to \u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022 down to \u2022\u2022, and the first part of \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 down to \u2022\u2022\u2022. Then I'd flesh out \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 with something better than what I moved down to \u2022\u2022\u2022, but still not good enough to qualify for \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022's \u201cWelcome to the 1%\u201d. I'd keep the <i>labels</i> the same: X is Working Poor, \u2022 is Slightly Ahead of the Game, \u2022\u2022 is Lower middle class, \u2022\u2022\u2022 is Middle class with property (or perhaps Upper middle class), \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 is Well-off, and \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 is \u201cWelcome to the 1%\u201d. But what they <i>mean</i> would shift downward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T22:25:58-07:00","id":1515987,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a>, I believe that when the table says that you &quot;got&quot; a place, it means you *own* the place (it's not rented, it's yours). In this case, I believe the table is more on par with the description and reality.<br /> <br /> X means that you don't have your own place nor vehicle, but you probably have somewhere to sleep (rented apartment, friend's house, whatever), you have an income , thay you practically use all of it each month. This also means you have *stuff*. You might have a cellphone, maybe a computer, clothes, etc. Small stuff.<br /> <br /> The other levels, just adds more properties, vehicles and savings/investments.<br /> <br /> I didn't remember M20 reaources were like that. This is much better than earlier editions, that required you to buy the background, or else you would have absolutely nothing. In M20, even without respurces you still can have basics things, like a phone, clothes and a laptop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T03:36:17-07:00","id":1516000,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> really glad to hear things are looking better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T06:00:14-07:00","id":1516004,"title":"","content":"Something that would be reasonable/likely/logical for a Mage character would be resources that don't seem to make sense. Example: A nearly broke Mage who has a large place to live in a city. We've all seen TV and film characters who have large living spaces like abandoned warehouses, a barge or similar non-yatch boat, abandoned sections of the subway, etc. <br /> <br /> Mages have ways of getting resources that don't fit in with normal economics. For people in the real world, it is very difficult to have a large living space without a large income and an excellent credit rating. Mages can skip to the thing they want/require without intermediate steps. <br /> <br /> For Mages we need a chopier way of defining resources that can represent the fantasy more closely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T07:06:38-07:00","id":1516008,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that there's also Debts. Part of my financial downfall, cited earlier, was that I actually lost <i>two </i>vehicles, both whole I was still making payments on them. I still have a couple of dots of Debts hanging over me too this day because of that <br /> <br /> I'm not aware of owning an apartment being a thing; last I checked, nearly everyone who lives in an apartment rents it from a landlord who owns the entire building. So \u2022 being that you own an apartment doesn't make sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T09:54:48-07:00","id":1516019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1516008#post1516008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not aware of owning an apartment being a thing; last I checked, nearly everyone who lives in an apartment rents it from a landlord who owns the entire building. So \u2022 being that you own an apartment doesn't make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200bNope. Owning a property is a thing. Maybe in some countries or regions it might be rare, but people do own apartments and especially houses.Where I live, people rent apartment directly from other people. There are no landlords owning an entire building.<br /> <br /> What would make no sense would be someone that have a paycheck that's enough to live (at least until next one) and not having a place to sleep. Shelter is a major need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 06-24-2023, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T16:06:21-07:00","id":1516046,"title":"","content":"I spoke specifically of owning <i>an apartment. </i>Not \u201ca property\u201d or \u201ca house\u201d; an apartment. Apartment <i>buildings </i>are owned; but I've never seen <i>individual apartments </i>in a building sold to their occupants. <br /> <br /> Also, the one- and two-dot levels speak of \u201cyou've got an apartment\u201d, which is at best about as to ownership: colloquially, someone who's renting an apartment speaks of \u201chaving an apartment\u201d. It isn't until the third dot that ownership is explicitly mentioned; and there, it's \u201cyou own or have significant equity in a house\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T01:08:42-07:00","id":1516071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta#post1514544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since pc's can simply use magick to help generate wealth, such as using entropy and time to help play the stock market, why would players want to take resources as a background and not invest in something different?</div> </div> </div> </div>This frees up time and effort in regard to Magick Effects that would be used to generate or secure resources and wealth.<br /> EArning money, creating resources, engaging in trade, and crafting item also helps hone and improve mundane skills. <br /> Generating wealth fairly and in a mudane way also helps secure social networks and group meetings, and is verifable proof of responsibiltiy, desire, ambition, and patience.<br /> In many completely or mostly mudane earnign and handling of money, resources, and valuebles is faster and more reliable compared to Magick Effects that can be used for these purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T03:19:56-07:00","id":1516084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1516046#post1516046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spoke specifically of owning <i>an apartment. </i>Not \u201ca property\u201d or \u201ca house\u201d; an apartment. Apartment <i>buildings </i>are owned; but I've never seen <i>individual apartments </i>in a building sold to their occupants.<br /> <br /> Also, the one- and two-dot levels speak of \u201cyou've got an apartment\u201d, which is at best about as to ownership: colloquially, someone who's renting an apartment speaks of \u201chaving an apartment\u201d. It isn't until the third dot that ownership is explicitly mentioned; and there, it's \u201cyou own or have significant equity in a house\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a cultural difference, but in Europe you can own apartments in an apartment buildings, actually most apartments will be bought during the construction of the building by future occupants, and then these are resold from owner to owner.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T05:52:56-07:00","id":1516095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1516046#post1516046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spoke specifically of owning <i>an apartment. </i>Not \u201ca property\u201d or \u201ca house\u201d; an apartment. Apartment <i>buildings </i>are owned; but I've never seen <i>individual apartments </i>in a building sold to their occupants.</div> </div> </div> </div>I lived in an apartment complex that sold its individual units to investors. I know of apartment complexes that run as condominiums in the US, Canada, and the UK. And I've heard of other systems of ownership in Denmark, Italy, and Ireland. So owning individual apartments is a thing. And it is a commonplace thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the one- and two-dot levels speak of \u201cyou've got an apartment\u201d, which is at best about as to ownership: colloquially, someone who's renting an apartment speaks of \u201chaving an apartment\u201d. It isn't until the third dot that ownership is explicitly mentioned; and there, it's \u201cyou own or have significant equity in a house\u201d. </div> </div> </div>This makes sense. Maybe specify that 0 in resources means an efficiency (a bathroom, a closet, and a bedsitting room with kitchenette) or a roommate. Actual homelessness could be a separate flaw.<br /> <br /> Logically, a Mage might have good resources and still be homeless. Think of wandering mages that never stay anyplace for more than a few weeks. Other mages might simply be outside the economy. And a few dead broke. But homelessness for a Mage is somewhat separate from resources.<br /> <br /> Also, a Mage might be destitute but have a place to stay. Both V and Gene Hackman's Lex Luthor made abandoned subway tunnels into comfortable homes. You say that's not realistic. I say we're talking about Mages. The <b>Mansion </b>merit already covered this. There is a background in <b>Adventure!</b> 1st edition that covers hideouts etc. It could be adapted to Mage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-25-2023, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T07:32:24-07:00","id":1516098,"title":"","content":"In that regard, I'd look at the Chantry/Construct Background as a baseline. If it's not pooled with other mages, it would represent a personal base of operations. That said, its X level would have to change, for the same reason why Resources X can't represent being homeless: if you actually have \u201cno place to call home\u201d, that should be a Flaw, not merely a failure to invest dots into a Background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T17:31:22-07:00","id":1516157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1516046#post1516046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spoke specifically of owning <i>an apartment. </i>Not \u201ca property\u201d or \u201ca house\u201d; an apartment. Apartment <i>buildings </i>are owned; but I've never seen <i>individual apartments </i>in a building sold to their occupants.<br /> <br /> Also, the one- and two-dot levels speak of \u201cyou've got an apartment\u201d, which is at best about as to ownership: colloquially, someone who's renting an apartment speaks of \u201chaving an apartment\u201d. It isn't until the third dot that ownership is explicitly mentioned; and there, it's \u201cyou own or have significant equity in a house\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used the word property to refer to houses or apartments. And yes, owning apartments is a thing. I own one. Probably this is a regional thing of where you live, but here we don't have landlords at all. Every apartment is owned by someone and when the owner wants to sell it, they announce on internet and etc.<br /> <br /> Most are sold to individual ppl while still on the ground, getting ready to build, as Asmodai said.<br /> <br /> About the background, I wouldn't say at all that someone with 0 resources, which have a paycheck and use almost all of it, doesn't have some place to sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T10:46:44-07:00","id":1516228,"title":"","content":"I have always found the Mage Resources background to be vague as I could never gauge what was appropriate from a rp perspective. My current sorcerer in my game has Resources 2 and is a professor of theology with his Academics 3 (master's degree) which I guess would make him an adjunct or non-tenured professor. Once he gets Academics 4 (doctorate degree), I will tell the ST that he would become a tenured professor and thus his Resources should increase to 3 to represent his increased salary. He also has Library 5 and thus he has a multitude of rare books and volumes that would have cost a pretty penny and I wondered if this would be possible for Resources 2.<br /> <br /> This also brings Alchemy into the discussion because you need either Sanctum or Resources to procures the materials needed, but there is no measure as to how many dots you need in these backgrounds for each dot in Alchemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","user":"Starcomet","date":". 06-27-2023, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T18:08:24-07:00","id":1516847,"title":"","content":"How much are Professors, tenure or not, paid? I always assumed they were paid roughly the same as teachers, and up here in Canada at least, ain't nobody teaching for the money...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T04:44:28-07:00","id":1516878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1516847#post1516847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much are Professors, tenure or not, paid? I always assumed they were paid roughly the same as teachers, and up here in Canada at least, ain't nobody teaching for the money...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most tenured college professors here in the States make a decent, not sumptuous, living. Some celebrity scholars teaching at elite schools do make far more impressive salaries. A few anomalous individuals make much more. Celebrity coaches that make large profits for their school by bringing the fans to the stadium get salaries that reflect how much money they make for the school. Certain individuals working for colleges sponsored by right-wing religious groups are also surprisingly well paid. One assumes scholarship has little to do with their pay packets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-01-2023, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T17:21:49-07:00","id":1516929,"title":"","content":"RE: Professors in the US<br /> <a href=\"https://acoup.blog/2023/04/28/collections-academic-ranks-explained-or-what-on-earth-is-an-adjunct/\" target=\"_blank\">This blog post</a> by Pete Devereaux from his blog A Collection of Unmitigated Pedantry may prove enlightening.<br /> <br /> In short, very few &quot;professors&quot; are tenured or tenure-track. The majority are adjuncts, that effectively operate in an academic gig economy. It's super fucked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T10:40:51-07:00","id":1517083,"title":"","content":"Indeed, there are few professors that are tenured and most are adjuncts who travel from school to school in many ways. Some professors do make a nice upper middle class salary, but this depends largely on the university/college in question, whether they have a doctorate or masters, adjunct or tenured, etc. They also tend to make money on the side from publishing books and doing academic research as well. In the U.S, professors tend to make a little more money than teachers at primary and secondary schools, but this largely requires they have a doctorate and be able to suck up to their department chair and the dean.<br /> <br /> Oh and my character is definitely not a professor for the money!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T16:39:31-07:00","id":1517119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1514544-what-s-the-point-of-the-resource-background-in-mta?p=1516157#post1516157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I used the word property to refer to houses or apartments. And yes, owning apartments is a thing. I own one. Probably this is a regional thing of where you live, but here we don't have landlords at all. Every apartment is owned by someone and when the owner wants to sell it, they announce on internet and etc.<br /> <br /> Most are sold to individual ppl while still on the ground, getting ready to build, as Asmodai said.<br /> <br /> About the background, I wouldn't say at all that someone with 0 resources, which have a paycheck and use almost all of it, doesn't have some place to sleep.</div> </div> </div> </div>In America, we call &quot;apartments that you own&quot; condominiums. Otherwise, they're always rented. Considering that a condo falls under two dots for Resources, I think it's pretty evident that your character doesn't &quot;own the apartment&quot; if they have a dot in the resource. They're clearly renting that.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, for zero dots in MtA revised, this is what it says:<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b&quot;X Flat busted: No job, no money, no prospects.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it's very evident that zero dots means that you're basically homeless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28074-doktor-von-zwitter","name":"Doktor von Zwitter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28074_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}